internal/provider/bytedance/astpb/

  Contains Go message types generated from ByteDance/Volcengine's published AST
  (Audio-Streaming Transport) protocol buffer definitions, used by the ByteDance
  provider's realtime audio transport. The .proto sources are ByteDance/
  Volcengine's; only the generated Go message types are vendored here. See
  internal/provider/bytedance/astpb/README.md for provenance and regeneration.

Go module dependencies are distributed under their own licenses (predominantly
Apache-2.0, MIT, and BSD-3-Clause); run `go-licenses report ./...` for the full,
current inventory. Notable direct dependencies include Gin (MIT), pgx (MIT),
go-redis (BSD-2-Clause), minio-go (Apache-2.0), prometheus/client_golang
(Apache-2.0), OpenTelemetry (Apache-2.0), modernc.org/sqlite (BSD-3-Clause),
and golang-jwt/jwt (MIT).
